    "perplexity": {
      "description": "God Says No is the fifth studio album by Monster Magnet, released in 2000 in Europe and 2001 in the United States on A&M Records. It finds the band moving further into polished hard rock and stoner rock territory, balancing heavy riffs and spacey textures with a more streamlined, song-oriented approach than some of their earlier work.\n\nThe album includes tracks such as “Melt,” “Heads Explode,” “Doomsday,” and the title song, and it runs just over an hour in length. God Says No was a commercial disappointment compared with Monster Magnet’s previous success, but it remains a notable entry in their catalog for its glossy production, hook-heavy songwriting, and the way it captures the band at a transitional point between underground cult status and broader rock ambition.",
